{"id":"brugger-thomet-mp9","slug":"brugger-thomet-mp9","name":"MP9","aliases":["MP9-M","TP9SF","Bt mp9","Bt tp9","MP9-FX","BT MP9-M","BT TP9SF","BT MP9-FX","TP9 Carbine","BT TP9 Carbine","Brugger & Thomet MP9","Brugger & Thomet TP9","Brügger & Thomet TMP","Brugger & Thomet TMP","Brügger & Thomet MP9-M","Brügger & Thomet TP9SF","Brügger & Thomet MP9-FX","Brügger & Thomet TP9 Carbine","Brügger & Thomet MP9"],"kind":"firearm","category":"pdws","subcategory":"Submachine gun","description":"The Brügger & Thomet MP9 (German: Maschinenpistole 9mm, lit. 'Machine pistol 9mm') is a submachine gun chambered for the 9×19mm Parabellum cartridge that is designed and manufactured by Brügger & Thomet.","development":"The MP9 is a development of the Steyr TMP, which was purchased from Steyr in 2001. Differences from the TMP include a stock that folds to the right side of the weapon, an integrated Picatinny rail, and a new trigger safety.\nThe MP9 is a selective-fire submachine gun. It uses 15, 20, 25, and 30 round transparent polymer detachable box magazines. It has three safeties: an ambidextrous safety/fire mode selector switch (manual safety), a trigger safety, and a drop safety.\nThe MP9 is made of polymer and is also corrosion-resistant. Its design and ease of operability allow the user to holster the weapon like a machine pistol or personal defense weapon for rapid deployment in self-defence.\nLater variants (TP9-N, TP9-US, MP9-N, MP45) feature new ambidextrous two/three-position selectors. The old Steyr style cross-bolt push button selectors are replaced with new \"HK\" style selectors.","facts":[],"specifications":[{"group":"Cartridge & Action","items":[{"label":"Cartridge","value":"9×19mm Parabellum"},{"label":"Cartridge","value":"6.5×25mm CBJ"},{"label":"Cartridge","value":".45 ACP (MP45)"},{"label":"Action","value":"Short recoil, locking rotating barrel"},{"label":"Rate of Fire","value":"900 RPM","numeric":900,"unit":"RPM"},{"label":"Muzzle Velocity","value":"400 m/s","nu